---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
import { GITHUB_URL, LINKEDIN_URL } from '../consts';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Senior RAN engineer building AI agents for network operations, on local models."
	pubDate={new Date('2026-10-03T12:00:00-05:00')}
>
	<p>
		I'm Gino Viloria, a telecommunications engineer from Barranquilla, Colombia. I've spent 15+
		years in 2G–5G radio access networks across Latin America and Japan, including the RF team that
		launched Rakuten Mobile's Open RAN network in Tokyo. Today I work on LTE/5G planning and
		optimization at WOM Colombia, where I built a parameter audit framework for ~30K Huawei cells.
	</p>
	<p>
		I'm moving into AI engineering, focused on <strong>agents for network operations</strong>:
		tool-calling LLMs that read KPIs and configuration, find the root cause and explain it, with a
		human approving any change.
	</p>
	<p>This blog is my lab notebook. Every post follows the same rules:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Runs on <strong>local models</strong> (Ollama), with no paid APIs.</li>
		<li><strong>Traced and measured</strong>: what failed and what fixed it, not just the final demo.</li>
		<li>The <strong>code is public</strong>; network data is fictional unless stated otherwise.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Currently: LangChain Academy (Introduction to LangChain completed) and preparing for the
		LangChain Certified Agent Engineer (LCAE) exam.
	</p>
	<p>
		Code on <a href={GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a> · let's talk on <a href={LINKEDIN_URL}>LinkedIn</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>
